  "root_cause": "In auth.py, the _ROLE_DISPATCH dictionary uses get(role, _default_access), which passes the function _default_access itself instead of calling it, causing roles not explicitly listed (like 'guest') to fall back to the default access function, which is not intended. This means 'guest' roles are not properly dispatched to guest_access().",
  "code_commitments": [
    "get_access must call the handler function to obtain the access dict",
    "The role dispatch must include 'guest' mapped to guest_access"
  ],
  "fix_strategy": "Update the get_access function to call the handler function immediately by adding parentheses, and add the 'guest' role to the _ROLE_DISPATCH dictionary with guest_access as its handler.",
